  Once the electric field has reached A, all the potential energy has been transformed in kinetic energy.
  There is no longer any difference in electric potential, equilibrium has been reached.
  Yet the electrons are still moving.

  Electrical speed is an ambiguous term that can refer without distinction to either drift velocity or speed of the electric field.
