      This explains what a high-quality component is and why people sometimes spend a considerable amount of money on them.
      Circuits are designed with ideal components. What we call the quality of a component (what makes it "good") is how close it is to ideal.
      So the higher the quality of the components, the closer the circuit is to its theoretical design --
      -- and the more predictable its behaviour.
      (Or: the poorer the quality of components, the more surprises -- note that surprises are not inherently bad.)
