    (2)  a current driven by a voltage source of alternating polarity.

  Here, in order to be consistent with ourselves, we'll go with (1) (even though the verb "to alternate" points more easily at (2)...).
  (Notice how the looser meaning of DC leads to the stricter meaning of AC and vice-versa.)

  The current from an AC generator can have pseudo-random variations (e.g. a guitar pickup) or it can be cyclic / periodic
